What does this code log?

```js
const count = 0;
console.log(count || 10, count ?? 10);
```

What does this log?

```js
const flag = new Boolean(false);
console.log(flag ? "yes" : "no", typeof flag);
```

What does this log?

```js
const user = { settings: { theme: "" } };
console.log([
  user.settings?.theme || "light",
  user.settings?.theme ?? "light",
  user.profile?.name ?? "anon",
]);
```

What does this log?

```js
const obj = {
  valueOf() { return 42; },
  toString() { return "obj"; },
};
console.log(obj + "", `${obj}`, String(obj));
```

What does this log?

```js
const d = new Date(0);
console.log(typeof (d + 1), d - 1);
```

What does this log?

```js
const temp = {
  [Symbol.toPrimitive](hint) {
    if (hint === "number") return 21;
    if (hint === "string") return "twenty-one";
    return "default";
  },
};
console.log(+temp, `${temp}`, temp + "", temp * 2);
```

What does `copy` look like after this runs?

```js
const original = { when: new Date(0), tags: new Map([["a", 1]]), note: undefined };
const copy = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(original));
```

What does this log?

```js
const calls = [];
const x = {
  valueOf() { calls.push("v"); return {}; },
  toString() { calls.push("s"); return "7"; },
};
console.log(x * 2, calls.join(""));
```

What do these two calls return?

```js
eval("{} + []");
eval("({} + [])");
```

This code runs as an ES module. What happens?

```js
const s = "hi";
s.extra = 1;
console.log(s.extra);
```

What does this log?

```js
const a = { n: 0, valueOf() { return ++this.n; } };
console.log(a == 1 && a == 2 && a == 3, a.n);
```
